				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7759545b-96dc-47d4-a968-79e281910b7c")
	)
	(text "Important: 6N137 output is inverted\n\nThe datasheet truth table shows:\n\nNano PWM HIGH → 6N137 output LOW\nNano PWM LOW  → 6N137 output HIGH\n\nThis is especially important for dead time. Your Arduino code must produce active-low PWM signals, so the safe condition is:\n\nNano high-side output = HIGH\nNano low-side output  = HIGH\n\nAfter the two optocouplers invert them:\n\nIR2112 HIN = LOW\nIR2112 LIN = LOW\n\nThat safely switches both MOSFETs off.\n\nDo not generate normal active-high complementary PWM with both Nano pins LOW during dead time. After the optocouplers, both IR2112 inputs would become HIGH, which could command both MOSFETs on and cause shoot-through."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 372.618 133.096 90)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e3588491-0e65-4356-9cb7-57dae0bb0497")
	)
